  "en": {
   "title": "Cimarron Mountain Club, 39 in of snow: today's depth on the upper slopes (12 November)",
   "description": "Cimarron Mountain Club, 39 in of snow: today's depth on the upper slopes (12 November). 42 in (106 cm): that is the snow on the upper slopes of …",
   "lede": "42 in (106 cm): that is the snow on the upper slopes of Telluride today. Deepest snow in the US West today: Telluride, about 42 in (106 cm) on the upper slopes (model). Second Cimarron Mountain Club, 39 in (98 cm); third Wolf Creek, 35 in (88 cm). Snow-covered ground in the US West: 57,757 sq mi (149,590 km²). Resorts with snow: 132 of 195. The model is right more often than a hunch, and less often than we would like.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Today's snow map",
     "p": [
      "Snow-covered area: 64,850 sq mi (167,960 km²) on 10 November, 57,757 sq mi (149,590 km²) today, 69,201 sq mi (179,230 km²) forecast for 15 November. The map is getting less white.",
      "Telluride by height, from our model: top 38 in (96 cm) (12,507 ft / 3,812 m), middle 2 in (6 cm) (10,620 ft / 3,237 m), base 0 in (0 cm) (8,734 ft / 2,662 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Rain up to the top?",
     "p": [
      "On Thursday 12 November the freezing level climbs to about 13,320 ft (4,060 m), above the top of the lifts at 11,355 ft (3,461 m): rain can fall even at the top.",
      "Rain on fresh snow makes it heavy and, after a cold night, icy: the days after are better for groomed runs than for powder.",
      "At about 10,584 ft (3,226 m), Cimarron Mountain Club has 3 in (8 cm) today; a normal 12 November has 7 in (19 cm) there.",
      "Only one winter in ten has more than 24 in (60 cm) on this date.",
      "A week ago the same spot had 5 in (12 cm).",
      "In past winters the best snow at Cimarron Mountain Club usually came mid-March / late March.",
      "Day by day at Cimarron Mountain Club: Saturday 14 November 2 in (6 cm); Sunday 15 November 0 in (1 cm).",
      "Height by height at Cimarron Mountain Club: 9,813 ft (2,991 m) 0 in (0 cm) on the ground, 5 in (12 cm) more in the next 7 days; 10,584 ft (3,226 m) 2 in (6 cm) on the ground, 5 in (13 cm) more in the next 7 days; 11,355 ft (3,461 m) 9 in (24 cm) on the ground, 6 in (14 cm) more in the next 7 days."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Station check",
     "p": [
      "The Beartown station (11,581 ft / 3,530 m) adds a real measurement: 30 in (76 cm) on the ground on 10 November. Ground check, Rat Creek station (11,680 ft / 3,560 m): 23 in (58 cm) on the ground on 10 November, 1 in (3 cm) new in 24 hours. Ground check, Red Mountain Pass station (11,060 ft / 3,371 m): 23 in (58 cm) on the ground on 10 November.",
      "Resort values: modelled, area-wide. Station values: measured, one point. Read them together."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Is this normal?",
     "p": [
      "Wolf Creek, 11,010 ft (3,356 m): 26 in (65 cm) today. That beats this date in 31 of the past 46 winters (usual: 9 in (23 cm)). A good start."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The forecast in short",
     "p": [
      "Forecast to 15 November: 6 in (16 cm) at Brian Head Resort, 5 in (13 cm) at Telluride and 4 in (11 cm) at Wolf Creek. Treat the later days with care.",
      "On 12 November the freezing level at Telluride sits at 10,039 ft (3,060 m) to 13,123 ft (4,000 m), over the top of the resort (12,507 ft / 3,812 m): rain or wet snow could fall on all slopes.",
      "Forecasts a few days ahead can change: look at the map again the day before you travel."
     ]
    }
